  privacy: "<!-- Counsel-pending Draft A policy copy; do not render this review marker. -->\n\n# Privacy Policy\n\n## The waitlist\n\nIf you join the early-access list, we collect **your email address** and your confirmation that\nyou are 18 or older and in the United States. If you arrive from a referral link we also record\nthe referral code and a privacy-safe source tag (which page or campaign sent you) — never shared\nwith any third party. That is everything. We do not collect your name, your location, or anything\nabout your skin — joining the list involves no photo and no scan.\n\n**Purpose:** to email you once when there is a build you can use.\n\n**Retention:** we delete what you gave us 90 days after we send you that invite, or 3 years after\nyou join if we never do, whichever comes first. An automated job enforces this — it is not a\npromise we have to remember to keep.\n\n**Unsubscribe:** every email carries a one-tap unsubscribe link, which deletes your record\noutright rather than flagging it as inactive.\n\nWe do not sell, lease, trade, or share your email address. The waitlist page loads no analytics,\nno advertising pixel, and no third-party script of any kind.\n\n## The app\n\nWhat we collect: face image (processed on-device, never uploaded), derived skin-appearance\nmetrics, and account information. We use the on-device read and saved derived data to show your\ncosmetic skin-appearance results, match you to cosmetic shades, suggest a brand-neutral cosmetic\nroutine, and show your own prior reads over time. TrueTone describes appearance only. It does not\nprovide a diagnosis or medical advice.\n\nWe never sell, lease, or trade biometric or health data. We do not share it with advertisers or\nanalytics providers. You can view and delete your data in-app at any time.\n\n## Contacting us\n\nTo ask what we hold about you, or to have it deleted, email **ayaankhan102004@gmail.com**.\n",
